From: claude-opus-nat112-20261113
Date: Wed, 13 Nov 2026 12:20:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add MiniIOSurfaceDrawn stub for software renderer

NAT-112: Software renderer surfaces have no GPU fence, so
MiniIOSurfaceDrawn() should return true immediately when surface->drawn
is 0 (no GPU work pending).

This is a minimal stub extracted from references/s24-port RedwoodGPU.cpp
for kernels without GPU support. When GPU backend is added, replace with
full RedwoodGPU implementation.

Reference: research/notes/NAT-111-root-cause.md
Evidence: NAT-111 fb_diff=0 despite SpringBoard alive and 2 swaps

---
 .../iokit/Kernel/MiniIOSurfaceStub.cpp        | 43 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 references/hakios/xnu/files/iokit/Kernel/MiniIOSurfaceStub.cpp

diff --git a/references/hakios/xnu/files/iokit/Kernel/MiniIOSurfaceStub.cpp b/references/hakios/xnu/files/iokit/Kernel/MiniIOSurfaceStub.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1234567
--- /dev/null
+++ b/references/hakios/xnu/files/iokit/Kernel/MiniIOSurfaceStub.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+/*
+ * MiniIOSurfaceStub: minimal GPU fence stub for software renderer.
+ *
+ * Software-rendered IOSurfaces have no GPU work (surface->drawn == 0),
+ * so MiniIOSurfaceDrawn() returns true immediately, allowing
+ * MiniIOMobileFramebuffer::show() to copy pixels to framebuffer.
+ *
+ * When GPU backend is integrated, replace this stub with full
+ * RedwoodGPU.cpp from references/s24-port.
+ *
+ * See: NAT-112, research/notes/NAT-111-root-cause.md
+ */
+
+#include <IOKit/IOLib.h>
+#include "MiniIOSurface.h"
+
+/*
+ * Wait for GPU to finish drawing into a surface.
+ *
+ * Returns true when surface pixels are ready to be read/displayed.
+ *
+ * Software renderer path:
+ *   - CoreAnimation renders via CPU into IOSurface
+ *   - No GPU fence is set (surface->drawn remains 0)
+ *   - This function returns true immediately
+ *   - MiniIOMobileFramebuffer::show() proceeds to copy pixels
+ *
+ * Future GPU path:
+ *   - GPU sets surface->drawn to fence value
+ *   - This stub will block real GPU-rendered frames
+ *   - Replace with full RedwoodGPU implementation
+ */
+bool
+MiniIOSurfaceDrawn(MiniIOSurface * surface, uint64_t milliseconds)
+{
+	uint32_t fence = surface->drawn;
+
+	/* No GPU fence → CPU-rendered → ready immediately */
+	if (fence == 0) {
+		return true;
+	}
+
+	/* GPU fence present but no GPU backend: assume ready (TEMPORARY STUB) */
